# AUROS protected set — hardening/protected.list
#
# "Do NOT remove anything in the protected set (bootc, the update path, greenboot, NetworkManager,
# systemd)." Check S10 is the gate for this in CI. This file is the build-time half, so that a bad
# edit fails at the point it happens rather than forty minutes later in the matrix.
#
# NOTE / ASSUMPTION: auros-recipes/schema/PROTECTED.md does not exist yet. When it does, IT is
# authoritative and this file should be regenerated from it rather than maintained in parallel.
#
# COLUMNS: severity <TAB> kind <TAB> target
#   fatal    absent => the build fails here. These are present on the upstream base already, so their
#            absence can only mean something in THIS build removed them.
#   pending  absent => reported loudly, build continues. These are installed by build steps owned by
#            other tasks (A4 update agent, A5 trust material) which may not have landed yet. CI check
#            S10 is the gate that stops an image missing them from ever being published; making this
#            script fail on them instead would mean one task's unlanded work blocks every build.
#
# KINDS:
#   cmd      on PATH
#   pkg      rpm -q says installed
#   unit     systemd knows the unit
#   path     exists on the filesystem
#   content  <file>::<extended-regex> — the file exists AND matches. Used where a path check would be
#            vacuous: /etc/containers/registries.d and policy.json both exist on the upstream base
#            already, and DECISIONS.md D8 is precisely about a policy that exists and verifies
#            nothing. Checking the directory is there would reproduce the bug it warns about.
#
fatal	cmd	bootc
fatal	cmd	systemctl
fatal	path	/usr/lib/systemd/systemd
fatal	pkg	NetworkManager
fatal	pkg	selinux-policy-targeted
fatal	path	/etc/selinux/config
pending	pkg	greenboot
fatal	path	/usr/lib/bootc/kargs.d
pending	unit	bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer
pending	path	/usr/lib/pki/containers
pending	content	/etc/containers/policy.json::sigstoreSigned
pending	content	/etc/containers/policy.json::ghcr.io/aarohkandy
